---
import Lamp from "@/layouts/Lamp.astro";
import { CONTACT } from "@/lib/site";
const mailto = `mailto:${CONTACT}?subject=Morse%20Lamp`;
---

<Lamp title="Support" description="Answers to the common Morse Lamp questions, and how to reach me.">
  <main class="prose-lamp flex-1 pt-12 sm:pt-16">
    <a href="/" class="text-sm text-fg-dim hover:text-fg">Morse Lamp</a>
    <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight">Support</h1>
    <p class="mt-4">
      Write to <a href={mailto}>{CONTACT}</a>. Say which phone you use and what you expected to
      happen; I answer personally.
    </p>

    <h2>Why is there no sound?</h2>
    <p>
      Turn the volume up: the drills show "Sound is off" while it sits at zero. The silent switch
      does not mute Morse Lamp. On Bluetooth headphones the tone can arrive a beat late; the lamp
      and the haptics are always on time, so trust them for rhythm.
    </p>

    <h2>How do I reset my progress?</h2>
    <p>
      Settings → Reset progress. The app asks you to confirm, then locks everything except K and
      M and forgets your measured rhythm. There is no undo.
    </p>

    <h2>What order do letters unlock in, and why?</h2>
    <p>
      Morse Lamp follows the Koch method: you start with K and M, drill only what you have
      unlocked, and the next character arrives when your set is solid. "Solid" means the newest
      character has at least 20 attempts in keying and 20 in listening, and your whole set is at
      90 % or better over its last 50 attempts. The app teaches the 26 letters and 10 digits, in
      the Koch order, with digits mixed in along the way. Weak characters come up more often.
    </p>

    <h2>Does it work offline?</h2>
    <p>Entirely. The app never connects to the internet, so there is nothing to be offline from.</p>
  </main>
  <footer class="mt-16 py-8 text-sm text-fg-dim">
    <nav aria-label="Footer" class="flex gap-6"><a href="/" class="hover:text-fg">Home</a><a href="/privacy" class="hover:text-fg">Privacy</a></nav>
  </footer>
</Lamp>
